# Spirit of the Labyrinth (Bot1's) and dredge (Bot2's Golgari Grave-Troll): "if a replacement effect would try to replace a
# card that you can't draw, that effect can't apply" (Spirit's ruling; CR 614.17c). Bot2 draws its card for turn 2, then
# Entombs the Troll and casts Ancestral Recall: its three draws can't happen, so dredge is not offered for any of them (Bot2 is
# asked nothing as the spell resolves). On turn 4 the draw for the turn is Bot2's first card of the turn, so dredge may
# replace it, and Bot2 dredges: six cards milled and the Troll back in hand.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Pearl
Spirit of the Labyrinth
Plains x4
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Sapphire
Entomb
Ancestral Recall
Swamp x3
Swamp
Golgari Grave-Troll
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Spirit of the Labyrinth.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Hand.Count = 8
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Entomb.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Search(Golgari Grave-Troll)
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot2)
Bot2.Pass
! Bot2.Accept
[T2 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot2.Hand.Count = 4
? Bot2.Graveyard = Ancestral Recall; Entomb; Golgari Grave-Troll
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
Bot2.Accept
[T4 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot2.Hand.Count = 5
Bot2.Hand.Golgari Grave-Troll.Power = 0
Bot2.Library.Count = 14
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 8
